++### Packed recurrent checkpoints
++
++Status: implemented. A caller can export several recurrent states during one
++prefill without splitting the query into separate model forwards. These outputs
++do not replace `final_state` and do not change the main attention output.
++
++Provide `checkpoint_state` and `checkpoint_offsets` together. All checkpoint
++tensors must be contiguous CUDA tensors on the query device. Offsets use the
++same integer dtype as `cu_seqlens`, or int64 for fixed-length input. The caller
++owns and retains the output buffers through execution and graph replay.
++
++With `checkpoint_indptr`, sequence `i` owns rows
++`[checkpoint_indptr[i], checkpoint_indptr[i+1])`. The ranges must partition
++`[0, P)` without overlap; empty ranges are allowed. Offsets within each range
++must be strictly increasing, positive multiples of 16, no greater than that
++sequence's length. For example, `indptr=[0,2,2,3]` and
++`offsets=[256,512,256]` export two states from sequence 0, none from sequence 1,
++and one from sequence 2. These GPU-resident ordering/range invariants are the
++caller's responsibility; no device-to-host validation is inserted into forward.
++
++Without `checkpoint_indptr`, the single-checkpoint interface is preserved:
++`P=N`, with one offset per sequence; offset zero disables that sequence's
++checkpoint. Exported states retain FP32 recurrence precision even if the
++requested final-state buffer is BF16.
++
